Description: Fix CVE-2026-12802 - allow CMS recipients to require a minimum AEAD tag size
 AuthEnvelopedData recipients did not enforce a caller-chosen AEAD authentication
 tag length floor, so an attacker could downgrade a GCM/CCM ICV to a weaker size.
 Adds CMSTagLengthException, getAEADMacLength/checkTagSize helpers, and
 setMinimumTagSize() on JCA/JCE recipients (Bc* get the check field as no-op
 unless set). Backport adapted for 1.77 which lacks AbstractRecipient used
 upstream - state and checks live on each recipient class / CMSUtils instead.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/bcgit/bc-java/commit/0fefa539e6ac5c66e1daee5a13b23d1d4769cc01
Bug: https://github.com/bcgit/bc-java/wiki/CVE%E2%80%902026%E2%80%9012802
Last-Update: 2026-08-06

